 "conclusion": [
  "Usage moved to NEAR Intents: it settled 83% of NEAR's DEX volume over the last 6 full months and $12.02B in the 90 days to 2026-11-09, 1.83× the 90 days before (T1, T2).",
  "Some of that value reaches NEAR holders, through buybacks rather than protocol fees. Since the fee switch of 2026-02-23, captured Intents revenue buys NEAR on the open market. In the 90 days to 2026-11-09 that was $5.0M, 27% of Intents' fees; NEAR's gas burn added $260.4K (C1). \"Buyback\" is DefiLlama's label for revenue swept as NEAR into NEAR's revenue wallets, held, not burned; on chain those wallets account for 98% of it, 33% in the front-end fund rather than the buyback multisig.",
  "It is small next to the token. Annualized, captured value is $21.4M, 0.45% a year of NEAR's $4.76B market cap. Over the same months NEAR's total supply grew 2.5% a year net of burns, about $117.0M a year at $3.63; the buyback is 17% of that. The bought-back NEAR is held (2.23M NEAR in buybacks.multisignature.near), not burned. If NEAR governance's HSP-029 cut (max issuance 2.5% → 1.6% over 24 months) runs its full ramp, the same buyback would cover 27% of net issuance.",
  "NEAR's weekly price does not move with Intents volume (r = 0.00 over 96 weeks, T4; with BTC's moves taken out, r = -0.03, p = 0.81, T4m), and agent commerce is tiny next to Intents (T7). Small tickets are not an edge case: 48% of sampled swap legs and 47% of withdrawals were under $50 (P1). Agent-size tickets into NEAR get a 1Click quote: 0.29–0.46% under $50 (T9, quotes of 2026-11-10 06:39Z).",
  "Read as an investment case: the usage half is supported by the record so far (T1 and T2 describe the past; the forward tests F1 and F2 check it on new data), value capture exists but covers about 17% of issuance, and the agent half is still an option. The case for the token is that the captured share grows faster than supply; we would call it made when the buyback reaches half of net issuance over a 90-day window."
 ],
